# Without this, `COPY . .` drags the host's node_modules into the image.
#
# That is not merely wasteful — it is why a build could pass locally and fail in
# CI. pnpm's symlinked store arrived pre-populated from the developer's machine,
# so a workspace package whose manifest was never COPYed in the deps stage still
# resolved. The image was built from host state rather than from the lockfile,
# and the first clean checkout is where that gets discovered.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Regenerated inside the image; copying a host build in can also
# poison it with paths that only exist on the developer's machine.
.next
**/.next
dist
**/dist
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
**/.turbo

# Secrets never belong in a layer, even one that is later discarded.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local infrastructure state.
infra/.data

.git
.github
coverage
**/coverage
.DS_Store
*.log
